  "id": "sensory-gating",
  "term": "sensory gating",
  "definition": "Sensory gating is the brain’s ability to reduce its response to incoming sensory information, including sights and sounds. This filtering helps a person screen out stimuli that are irrelevant, repetitive, or without meaning.",
